  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want to keep my one-to-one MPs apart from my multi-participant MPs and read and answer the group ones like topics, so that group conversations stop drowning in my private exchanges.\n\nOperator decision 2026-10-28: multi-participant MPs (\"MP multiples\") are like topics of their own, but private; their reading and participation experience comes close to public topics. A setting chooses \"Tout en un\" (DEFAULT: today's single list, unchanged UX) or \"Deux listes\"; with two lists, a switch at the top of the Messages screen: \"MP\" / \"MP multiples\".\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Setting** (Réglages, section Messages): \"Affichage des MP\": \"Tout en un\" (default) / \"Deux listes\". New key; absent = \"Tout en un\", so nothing changes for anyone who does not opt in.\n- **Two lists:** a segmented control at the top of the MP list (LOT-126 (#217)): \"MP\" (one-to-one) and \"MP multiples\" (group). Each segment shows its own unread count; the tab / sidebar badge stays the total.\n- **Group detection:** `PrivateMessageThread.isGroup` (HFRModels, LOT-023): HFR prints `<span title=\"<pseudos>\">Interlocuteurs multiples</span>` in `sujetCase6` for group threads (HFR-PROTOCOL.md §6c, fixtures `R04`, `R08-2`, `R13u1`). Legacy does the same test (`MPListView.swift:376-377`, `Classes/HFRMPViewController.m:134`).\n- **Paging:** no server-side filter of the MP list is known; the split is client-side over the pages loaded. A segment whose loaded pages hold no thread loads the next page (bounded, stops at the last page) rather than showing an empty list while more exist. Any server filter needs a capture first, never a guess.\n- **Group rows look like topic rows:** title, participants (tooltip names, `interlocutors`), replies, last post, pages; unread marker as topics.\n- **Group thread reading and participation like a public topic:** it opens in the topic reader with the topic features as their lots land (page navigator LOT-110 (#201), first-unread LOT-111 (#202), message actions LOT-087 (#179), quote and multi-quote LOT-086 (#178), quick reply LOT-153 (#243)), replying through LOT-128 (#219). List here which topic features apply to MPs and which do not (flags do not exist for MPs), with the legacy source for each.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: operator decision 2026-10-28 (C)\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `HFRswift/Swift/MPListView.swift:359-377` (`hasMultipleInterlocutors`), `:773-780`, `Classes/HFRMPViewController.m:134-135, 234`\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-171-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-126 (#217): MP list screen\n- LOT-119 (#210, in PR #292): settings screen\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- Fixture `R13u1` (group row) exists. A paged MP list mixing group and one-to-one threads over several pages, and a group thread page with three or more participants, are *pending capture* if the spec needs them (new `host: mac` capture issue, never hand-built, LESSONS 35-36).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Default (\"Tout en un\"): the MP list is exactly LOT-126's (test).\n- [ ] \"Deux listes\": the switch shows only one-to-one or only group threads; each segment's unread count is right on the fixtures.\n- [ ] A segment never shows \"empty\" while later pages may hold matching threads.\n- [ ] A group thread opens in the topic reader and offers the topic features listed in the spec.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
